\"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Robert Pająk\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Mike Blum\\n\\n## Action Items\\n\\n- Robert:\\n\\n  - Work with GC to set up a maintainers mailing list for OSS-Fuzz notifications and ensure appropriate access for Go SIG maintainers.\\n\\n  - Consider manual recreation of older OSS-Fuzz issues if needed; revisit auto GitHub issue filing after triage process matures.\\n\\n  - Take ownership of otelhttp issue [#7254](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254); draft a document clarifying error marking approach and semconv alignment.\\n\\n  - Enable GitHub signature releases for OTel Go; update releasing docs; ensure artifacts are uploaded at release time and signatures published. Reference: [sig-security #164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164).\\n\\n- Damien:\\n\\n  - Open an issue to kick off an audit of the otelhttp API for stabilization and coordinate reviews.\\n\\n- David (dashpole):\\n\\n  - Monitor semconv RPC stabilization efforts; once stable, drive otelgrpc module stabilization.\\n\\n  - Sync with Josh regarding gRPC team engagement; explore KubeCon conversations if feasible.\\n\\n- Mike:\\n\\n  - Iterate on the otel Explorer Go docs schema:\\n\\n    - Align with OTEL semantic conventions.\\n\\n    - Ensure Weaver compatibility.\\n\\n    - Provide a JSON Schema (or CUE) for validation.\\n\\n    - Consider linking instrumentations to existing semconv references.\\n\\n- Tyler:\\n\\n  - Assign relevant GitHub tasks/issues from this meeting.\\n\\n  - Confirm KubeCon schedule and cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; share booth details with the community.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"robert paj ą k david ashpol mike blum action item 