[], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3131552355963499, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09607336513764277, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8196796, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> Could you turn your gist into a test that can run on CI, and add it to this PR?\\n\\nSure, I'd be happy to.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T07:42:26Z\\n\\n> ```go\\n\\n> }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n>           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n>           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> ```\\n\\nI believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\nI'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing data race\\\". Rather, it removes unnecessary code that has unintended side effects.\\n\\ne.g., The defer restoration discards any context modifications made within the `otelgin` middleware chain (including downstream handlers).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T07:47:23Z\\n\\n> > ```go\\n\\n> > }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n> >           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n> >           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> > ```\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing d