bot 2025 10 14t07 50 11z sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"998f12a39803f3d9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31235028132314663, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1080525876044952, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7890449, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Seek more engagement from gRPC; attempt in-person conversations at KubeCon if possible. David will sync with Josh on outreach.\\n\\n- Conclusion: Not likely to stabilize this year; set a goal to finalize a strategy next year once semconv progress is clearer.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [Stabilization of otelgrpc](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8078)?\\n\\n  - Related: [https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/8265)  \\n\\n  - We need the semconv to stabilize  \\n\\n  - There needs to be involvement from gRPC to progress this  \\n\\n  - [David] Update: I’m told that the SIG is active and is working towards stabilization. Not sure if gRPC is involved.  \\n\\n### Stabilization of otelhttp\\n\\n- Damien proposed starting an API audit for otelhttp to move towards stabilization.\\n\\n- A known bug (issue #7254) may be the only blocker; it’s a behavioral change around how errors are marked (events vs attributes) and interacts with semconv/spec wording.\\n\\n- Agreement:\\n\\n  - Begin the API review.\\n\\n  - Robert will take ownership of #7254 and draft a document clarifying interpretation and proposed resolution.\\n\\n  - The existence of bugs does not inherently block stabilization; they can be fixed post-stabilization if changes are non-breaking or properly versioned.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- Blocker (only one I think): [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254)  \\n\\n### OTel Explorer Go docs\\n\\n- Mike outlined a project to revamp the OTEL registry/explorer with a schema that documents spans/metrics emitted by instrumentations, aiming to render via Hugo and enable static analysis across Go SDKs and contrib modules.\\n\\n- Tyler’s feedback:\\n\\n  - Strong requirement: align schema with semantic conventions and ensure it’s compatible with Weaver (to enable validation and transformations across versions).\\n\\n  - Consider providing a JSON Schema (or CUE) for validation and potentially linking to existing semconv definitions to keep the spec concise.\\n\\n  - Scope can include eBPF/auto-instrumentation; representation should still fit the schema as long as it maps to OTEL signals.\\n\\n- Mike will iterate on the schema, explore Weaver integration, and coordinate with SIGs as needed.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n  - Context: [https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000](https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000)  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"seek more engag from grpc attempt in person convers at kubecon if possibl david will sync with josh on outreach conclus not like to stabil this year set a goal to final a strategi next year onc semconv progress is clearer refer stabil of otelgrpc http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8078 relat http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 http github com grpc grpc go issu 8265 we need the semconv to stabil there need to be involv from grpc to progress this david updat i m told that the sig is activ and is work toward stabil not sure if grpc is involv stabil of otelhttp damien propos start an api audit for otelhttp to move toward stabil a known bug issu 7254 may be the onli blocker it s a behavior chang around how error are mark event v attribut and interact with semconv spec word agreement begin the api review robert will take ownership of 7254 and draft a document clarifi interpret and propos resolut the exist of bug doe not inher block stabil they can be fix post stabil if chang are non break or proper version refer blocker onli one i think http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 otel explor go doc mike outlin a project to revamp the otel registri explor with a schema that document span metric emit by instrument aim to render via hugo and enabl static analysi across go sdks and contrib modul tyler s feedback strong requir align schema with semant convent and ensur it s compat with weaver to enabl valid and transform across version consid provid a json schema or cue for valid and potenti link to exist semconv definit to keep the spec concis scope can includ ebpf auto instrument represent should still fit the schema a long a it map to otel signal mike will iter on the schema explor weaver integr and coordin with sig a need refer context http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"5449cc5184194ce6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31218849704994334, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12003181007134762, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7605541, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Description\\n\\n`otelhttp` only uses `span.RecordError(err)` when `errType` is not empty\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/otelhttp/transport.go#L132-L140\\n\\nBut `ErrorType` method never returns an empty attribute.\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/httptrace/otelhttptrace/internal/semconv/httpconv.go#L443-L458\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nI don't have a preference on whether we should record `error.type` with `exception.type` at the same time. But the comment and the logic here seem conflicted. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (15)\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-04-23T08:03:12Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 descript descript otelhttp onli us span recorderror err when errtyp is not empti http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http otelhttp transport go l132 l140 but errortyp method never return an empti attribut http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http httptrace otelhttptrac intern semconv httpconv go l443 l458 expect behavior i don t have a prefer on whether we should record error type with except type at the same time but the comment and the logic here seem conflict sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 discuss 15 dmathieu 2025 04 23t08 03 12z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"67607a2c8d579c3a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3114787455963499, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09607336513764277, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8140913, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:36: File removed: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n```\\n\\n----\\n\\nCurrently, I cannot determine whether this is a flaw in Go itself or if users are required to manually execute `RemoveAll()`. I have tried submitting [this issue](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455) to the official Go team to see if there will be any updates.\\n\\nThe following situations exist (tested and confirmed):\\n\\n1. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, but did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will be unable to delete the files;\\n\\n2. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, and manually called `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files;\\n\\n3. We executed `request.WithContext()` after executing `request.ParseMultipartForm,` and did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-03T13:24:52Z\\n\\nGiven that this [issue](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946#issuecomment-3028290240) currently lacks an official solution from the [Go team](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455), we need to find an appropriate workaround ourselves.\\n\\nMy suggestion is to proceed with the solution proposed in this [PR](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609) (also the consistent approach suggested by @zihuyishi and @akats7).  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 36 file remov var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 current i can not determin whether this is a flaw in go itself or if user are requir to manual execut removeal i have tri submit this issu http github com golang go issu 74455 to the offici go team to see if there will be ani updat the follow situat exist test and confirm 1 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform but did not manual call removeal on the new request it will be unabl to delet the file 2 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform and manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the file 3 we execut request withcontext after execut request parsemultipartform and did not manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the file flc1125 2025 07 03t13 24 52z given that this issu http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 issuecom 3028290240 current lack an offici solut from the go team http github com golang go issu 74455 we need to find an appropri workaround ourselv my suggest is to proceed with the solut propos in this pr http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 also the consist approach suggest by zihuyishi and akats7\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5af8802d20a0e988\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3013351698695532, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08409414267079032, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8082309, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"However, this approach will also introduce additional side effects, for which there is currently no better solution.  \\n\\n**Impact:**  \\n\\nAssuming our middleware is wrapped in the following manner: `m1(m2(otel-middleware(m3(fn))))`,  \\n\\nwhere `m1` and `m2` internally implement operations such as `request.ParseMultipartForm(1)`. Due to the effect of `RemoveAll` in `otel-middleware`,  \\n\\nthere may be cases where they repeatedly create `request.MultipartForm` resources, resulting in additional memory allocations.\\n\\nOf course, we can also choose not to handle it, but we need to remind users to process `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`.\\n\\n----\\n\\nI'd like to hear your opinions: @akats7 @open-telemetry/go-approvers \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `area: instrumentation`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `bug`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `instrumentation: otelgin`\\n\\n- 2024-11-21T12:21:58Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:45Z · **cross-referenced** by Yiling-J ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T08:06:05Z · **marked_as_duplicate** by dmathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"howev this approach will also introduc addit side effect for which there is current no better solut impact assum our middlewar is wrap in the follow manner m1 m2 otel middlewar m3 fn where m1 and m2 intern implement oper such a request parsemultipartform 1 due to the effect of removeal in otel middlewar there may be case where they repeat creat request multipartform resourc result in addit memori alloc of cours we can also choos not to handl it but we need to remind user to process c request multipartform removeal i d like to hear your opinion akats7 open telemetri go approv sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston timelin 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx area instrument 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx bug 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx instrument otelgin 2024 11 21t12 21 58z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 4588 2025 01 13t13 45 45z cross referenc by yile j http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 2025 07 02t08 06 05z mark _ a _ duplic by dmathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5b39be36d40588b5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3005512098695532, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08409414267079032, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8056177, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ee5caba072c6dc26\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2991472698695532, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08409414267079032, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8009379, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"*   David also mentioned ongoing work on exponential histograms and a simpler \\\"last value\\\" PR that shares code with the histogram one.\\n\\n*   Tyler expressed a strong desire to merge the histogram reservoir PR in the current milestone due to its significant performance improvement and encouraged attendees to review it.\\n\\n**6. Milestone Check-in and Release Goals**\\n\\n*   Tyler conducted a check-in on the v1.39.0 milestones for [Otel](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/milestone/74) and [Contrib](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/milestone/33).\\n\\n*   **Exposed Temporality Selector Function PR:** Tyler noted that a previous SIG meeting concluded this PR was API pollution and should be closed. He will draft a comment and close it today.\\n\\n*   **Simple Span Processor (Tracing):** This PR needs another round of reviews but is considered straightforward and should remain in the milestone.\\n\\n*   **OTLP Metric GRPC Exporter Metrics:** This PR has been open for a while and needs more iteration. It might be moved out of the current milestone if a release push occurs.\\n\\n*   **Metrics SDK Standard Out Metrics Exporter & Standard Log Exporter:** Both PRs lack follow-up from their original authors and significant work is still needed. They are candidates for being bumped from the milestone.\\n\\n*   **Overall Release Strategy:** Tyler proposed making a release before KubeCon (less than a month away) and urged everyone to prioritize reviews for the critical PRs to achieve this goal.\\n\\n**7. KubeCon Discussion**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** asked if there was anything specific to announce or discuss at KubeCon.\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** mentioned the extended attributes merge in specification and product as something he'd like to highlight, though it's not ready.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** expressed interest in showcasing the new observability features.\\n\\n*   David suggested working towards a stable release of the HTTP instrumentation in Contrib. Tyler agreed it was a good idea but noted the significant work involved due to existing \\\"cruft\\\" and potential needs for API restructuring.\\n\\n**8. Tyler's Side Project (OTLP Exporter Error Types)**\\n\\n*   Tyler shared that he's been working on introducing new, custom error types for OTLP exporters to provide clearer, more unified error messages. This involves distinguishing between HTTP/gRPC errors, partial errors, and warnings. He has a prototype integrated for Otel Trace gRPC. While not critical, it improves observability and user understanding of errors.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"david also mention ongo work on exponenti histogram and a simpler last valu pr that share code with the histogram one tyler express a strong desir to merg the histogram reservoir pr in the current mileston due to it signific perform improv and encourag attende to review it 6 mileston check in and releas goal tyler conduct a check in on the v1 39 0 mileston for otel http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go mileston 74 and contrib http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib mileston 33 expos tempor selector function pr tyler note that a previous sig meet conclud this pr wa api pollut and should be close he will draft a comment and close it today simpl span processor trace this pr need anoth round of review but is consid straightforward and should remain in the mileston otlp metric grpc export metric this pr ha been open for a while and need more iter it might be move out of the current mileston if a releas push occur metric sdk standard out metric export standard log export both pr lack follow up from their origin author and signific work is still need they are candid for be bump from the mileston overal releas strategi tyler propos make a releas befor kubecon less than a month away and urg everyon to priorit review for the critic pr to achiev this goal 7 kubecon discuss david ashpol ask if there wa anyth specif to announc or discus at kubecon robert paj ą k mention the extend attribut merg in specif and product a someth he d like to highlight though it s not readi tyler yahn express interest in showcas the new observ featur david suggest work toward a stabl releas of the http instrument in contrib tyler agre it wa a