{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"`opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254` is **closed as completed**. It was closed by pellared on **2026-01-13**, assigned to milestone **v1.40.0** (which is itself closed). The issue had been linked to contrib PR **#8386** immediately before closure. [SRC-ISSUE-02; SRC-MILE-04]\n\nThe underlying bug was that `otelhttp`’s new-semconv path could not record an error because its `ErrorType` behavior conflicted with the `RecordError` guard. The discussion aligned toward following the semantic conventions: for terminating errors, set `error.type` and span error status rather than unconditionally emitting an exception event; `RecordError` remains relevant for non-terminating/retry scenarios. [SRC-ISSUE-02]"}}
